# Gemtext v1.1.0

I’ve released a small update to Gemtext[i]. At the moment, I’m working on adding Spartan protocol[ii] support to Rogallo[iii], and to do this I need to handle a small extension it makes to Gemtext.

=> https://gemtext.davep.dev/ [i]
=> https://portal.mozz.us/spartan/spartan.mozz.us/ [ii]
=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/ [iii]

While Spartan is quite different from Gemini in the underlying protocol, it uses Gemtext as the default/standard markup language, but with one small difference. To allow uploaded data that is initiated by the markup, rather than by the server, there is a =: line type. In some respects, this is similar to type 7 items in Gopher maps.

Rather than spin up a whole new library just to support this one small difference, and rather than do some special-case nonsense in Rogallo itself, I’ve added optional (and turned on by default) support for =:. When encountered, this results in a SpartanPrompt[i] object, which simply inherits from a Link[ii].

=> https://gemtext.davep.dev/gemtext/#gemtext.SpartanPrompt [i]
=> https://gemtext.davep.dev/gemtext/#gemtext.Link [ii]

Any code that doesn’t require this feature can turn it off with the with_spartan_support parameter[i].

=> https://gemtext.davep.dev/gemtext/#gemtext.Gemtext(with_spartan_support) [i]

